# ai.schema — who may set each key of the `ai` subsystem (see w-conf.md).
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>   scope: system | user | both
#
# The assistant is a per-user tool with a machine-wide default, so most keys are
# `both`: the admin sets what a fresh account gets, and each user overrides it —
# that is exactly what `w-ai profile use` does when it writes ~/.config/w/ai.conf.

# ── Active selection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HOST	both
PROVIDER	both
MODEL	both
MODE	both
MCP_PROFILE	both
OLLAMA_HOST	both

# ── Provider → env-var mapping ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendor data, not a preference: it says which environment variable a provider's
# CLI expects, so a user file has no business redefining it (a wrong mapping would
# silently stop passing the key). New providers arrive with the vendor layer.
# A GLOB row, so a provider added to the vendor layer tomorrow arrives already
# declared instead of silently unconstrained.
PROVIDER_ENV_*	system

# ── Per-tool switches (W_AI_TOOL_*) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `both` on purpose. These decide which privileged tools are OFFERED to the model;
# they are UX, not the security boundary — every Tier-2 tool still goes through
# pkexec + polkit and raises W's own auth window regardless of any switch
# (ai-integration.md §3). So a user may narrow their own assistant's surface, and
# the admin sets the machine default. Tightening this to `system` would be a
# policy change, not a refactor — do it deliberately, if ever.
W_AI_TOOL_DNS	both
W_AI_TOOL_FIREWALL	both
W_AI_TOOL_FWUPD	both
W_AI_TOOL_PACMAN	both
W_AI_TOOL_APPLY	both
W_AI_TOOL_PACKS	both
W_AI_TOOL_UPDATE	both
W_AI_TOOL_LOCALE	both
W_AI_TOOL_MAINTAIN	both
W_AI_TOOL_HOSTNAME	both
W_AI_TOOL_TIMEZONE	both
W_AI_TOOL_NTP	both
W_AI_TOOL_POWER	both
W_AI_TOOL_SYNC	both
W_AI_TOOL_RUN	both

# ── ai-extra features (written by `w-ai features set`) ───────────────────────
# Per-user by design: they live in ~/.config/w/ai-features.conf so they survive a
# profile switch, and they cost only that user's own resources (an embedding model
# in their session's VRAM budget).
W_AI_SEARCH_PROVIDER	both
W_AI_EMBED	both
W_AI_EMBED_MODEL	both
W_AI_EMBED_URL	both
W_AI_EMBED_KEEPALIVE	both
